db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{12}}{13}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513693} {:answer/id #uuid "69f7fd71-6066-58ff-973d-5a24b0715dc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{14}}{14}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513816} {:answer/id #uuid "a01e6e97-6d87-5937-8e57-076aaa390207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{12}}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513942} {:answer/id #uuid "a8adc543-25c4-55be-8081-e8857819cce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{14}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513971} {:answer/id #uuid "f56d5cb2-21a5-51fe-8738-17f8affe9a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13{x}^{14}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69f7fd71-6066-58ff-973d-5a24b0715dc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{14}}{14}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513816} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8fbc5ea-5d9e-52eb-88d3-b4d6971c6c74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c1117fb-96ed-5032-8c50-48772b44cf5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-113668" :question/problem "Calculate $F(x)$ given that $f(x)={x}^{13}$ and ${F}^{′}(x)=f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{′}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe apply the power rule with $n=13$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{13}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{13+1}}{13+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{14}}{14}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{14}}{14}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{14}}{14})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{14}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{14})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{14}\\cdot 14\\,{x}^{13} & = \\\\ {x}^{13}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25425771-e7b7-59e7-a21c-34da79a147e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{1/2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513636} {:answer/id #uuid "46f4c2a1-30c4-58bc-a872-acf707c7f214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}^{5/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513723} {:answer/id #uuid "bf5da9ff-937c-53a4-b1fa-cc6b757fbfad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{1/2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514037} {:answer/id #uuid "dae23439-686a-536f-8883-85442f6a6ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{1/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514104} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7a9df8-4ded-54ff-9dd7-df5316a89579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2{x}^{5/2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25425771-e7b7-59e7-a21c-34da79a147e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{1/2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513636} :answer-field/id #uuid "a255f30f-2d4d-5a18-8010-7066f9da2d12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ce88619-593c-543d-be7b-78867655bb11" :question/math-academy-id "q-113703" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3/2}}$ and that ${F}^{′}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{′}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{3/2}}={x}^{-3/2}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3/2+1}}{(-\\frac{3}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/2}}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}+C \\\\  & =-2{x}^{-1/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{1/2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514388 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85af4ca3-5e66-522a-9e5a-6efb1c7114ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e343d0-9e3d-57b4-a7bc-fc9b2686c5b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513556} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2855e0-fb0a-5301-b062-4ac8a822906c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3/2}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513749} {:answer/id #uuid "81cf656b-bd3c-5484-968b-6e7bc93c98ad"